ure and longlisted for the 2007 International ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... This consolidation was desirable to publishers as it \\\"created the impression of a group by gathering together under a single label authors who had nothing, or very little, in common\\\" (Casanova 2004:120). As Kazuo Ishiguro remarked of the influence of Salman Rushdie's Booker Prize win on ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\" ... They kept the name Booker when they created the new Man Booker International Prize, but dropped it for the Man Asia Literary Prize.\\n\\nIn Australia, we have The Australian/Vogel Award for an unpublished first manuscript: a collaboration between a newspaper and a health foods company. The effect ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... Louis Post-Dispatch, Newsday, London Evening Standard, Time Out (London), San Jose Mercury News\\n* Finalist, National Book Critics Circle Award, 2003, 1995, 1991, 1985\\n* 2006 Finalist, Pulitzer Prize for Fiction\\n* 2010 Elected Member, American Academy of Arts and Letters\\n* 2014 Man Booker Prize (longlist)\\n* 2014 California Book Awards ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Powers\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first