\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... A selection of his poetry is collected in Desire Never … Read More\\n\\nColm Toíbín\\n\\nColm Toíbín is the author of six novels, including The Master, winner of the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award and shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, as well as winner of the LA Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... His debut novel, The Milk Chicken Bomb, was published by Coach House Books in 2007, named a finalist for the Amazon / Books in Canada First Novel Award, and long-listed for the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award. As a musician (guitar, shouting) he has written, recorded and toured ... \",\"title\":\"https://wordfest.com/2017/news/meet-your-festival-hosts/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... Times Book Prize (Fiction) WINNER 2011\\n\\nLos Angeles Times Book Prizes WINNER 2011\\n\\nNational Book Critics Circle Awards WINNER 2010\\n\\nPulitzer Prize WINNER 2011\\n\\nIMPAC Dublin Literary Award FINALIST 2012\\n\\nPEN/Faulkner Award for Fiction FINALIST 2010\\n\\n21 Books You've Been Meaning to Read\",\"title\":\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/201020/a-visit-from-the-goon-squad-by-jennifer-egan/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... He received several awards for his work, such as the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award (1997) and the International Nonino Prize (2011).\\n\\nDavid Gaub McCullough (1933–2022)\\n\\n\\\"Writing is thinking. To write well is to think clearly. That's why it's so hard.\\\"\\n\\n― \\\"\\n\\nDavid G. McCullough was ... \",\"title\":\"https://torontopubliclibrary.typepad.com/bookbuzz/2022/12/in-memoriam-authors-who-passed-away-in-2022.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"9199d523ef730e09334cd964962da67f113bc2784a0b337b824b2a4b5fefd181\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"9303521d46975614a1baad4abef9a1547a66899032bde582d90e0a75a53a74a7\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Dublin Literary Award IMPAC founded 1996\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2016, the award was significantly reconfigured, and is now given annually to a single book in English translation, with a £50,000 prize for the winning title, shared equally between author and translator. The award has been known as the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_n